      "id": "3npma8m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12. Solutions & Concentration"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Electrochemistry deals with the interconversion of chemical energy and electrical energy via oxidation-reduction reactions.",
        "Solutions and concentration units like molarity, molality, and normality form the foundation for quantitative chemical analysis.",
        "Nuclear chemistry encompasses nuclear decay, half-life calculations, and radioactive isotopes used in medicine and energy.",
        "Industrial processes such as Haber's process and the Contact process rely heavily on specific catalysts and optimal operating conditions.",
        "Environmental pollution and gas testing are crucial qualitative topics frequently featured in competitive examinations."
      ],
      "id": "swgqkhg"
    },
